            <ArticleTitle>Efavirenz in an obese HIV-infected patient--a report and an in vitro-in vivo extrapolation model indicate risk of underdosing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1381-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3851/IMP2107</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Here, we report suboptimal efavirenz exposure in an obese patient treated with the standard 600 mg dose. Tripling the dose allowed attainment of therapeutic efavirenz concentrations. We developed an in vitro-in vivo extrapolation model to quantify dose requirements in obese individuals. Obesity represents a risk factor for antiretroviral therapy underdosing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
